well sarah the politics here is  gathering pace after those very dramatic  events  last week which saw the capitol building  stormed by  trump's supporters now the democrats  were hoping  to introduce a resolution into the house  calling as you heard on mike pence the  vice president to introduce the 25th  amendment which would force uh donald  trump from  office it's basically an amendment to  the constitution which if a president is  physically  or mentally incapable of dispensing his  duties  uh he has to get out of the way in this  case of course it would be his mental  capacity  to be president of the united states  they were hoping for unanimity  that was blocked by the republicans so  what's happened now you've seen  the adjournment it will go back uh to  the floor tomorrow at 9 00 a.m where  there'll be  a vote on it and we'll see whether it  passes then  in the meantime we understand they've  also introduced a resolution  for impeachment against donald trump  that will be voted on we think  on wednesday it just needs a simple  majority and if that happens of course  donald trump will be in the ignominious  position of being  the first president ever to be impeached  twice um of course there are big  questions about the timetable of all of  that  it will get through the house of  representatives but what happens when it  gets to  the senate of course by the time it's  actually dealt with  donald trump will no longer be the  president of the united states  the senate doesn't reconvene until the  19th of january conventionally what  happens is the articles of impeachment  go to the senate they sit on it for a  day and then it goes for the floor  which would be the 20th of january the  day of the inauguration when  president-elect  joe biden becomes the next president of  the united states  interestingly one theory is that they  may sit on those articles of impeachment  and nancy pelosi won't push them over to  the senate  until joe biden has had his first 100  days he can choose the people he wants  to surround himself with  and also get his agenda off the ground  without it being overshadowed by the  specter  of uh donald trump and the accusations  against him of  treason high crimes and misdemeanors
 

